  "proof": [
    "36 actual pocket-sdram-staging dependency files contain no of_gpu.h dependency; firmware/api/of.h:82 explicitly excludes per-app GPU header.",
    "Pocket boot.c:101-109 defines only reset/status/DMA/texture-flush registers. Its sole GPU operation sequence351-361 soft-resets, waits DMA_BUSY, clears DMA source/length, flushes texture, ring-resets. It uploads no commands or ring pointer.",
    "Pocket video.c:1215 only reads GPU_FENCE_REACHED_REG. OS regs.h exposes that fence register; kernel loader and OS files have no GPU command ring submission helpers.",
    "Chip32 loader runs on Pocket host, selects/loads core and host reset/init; no GPU ring interface.",
    "Existing isolated SM64 INI selects ELF=sm64.elf directly; no menu app precedes it.",
    "Current built firmware ELF/MIF/OS hashes match historical firmware-artifacts receipt and qualified physical MIF/OS hashes."
  ],
  "compatibility_limits": [
    "This is source/dependency/artifact audit, not a fresh full-boot simulation.",
    "Every additional app/menu/diagnostic bundled into a reduced-ring profile must use the negotiated-capacity SDK or be independently proven not to submit GPU commands.",
    "Do not promote reduced-ring hardware to normal profiles with legacy app binaries.",
    "Keep writes to GPU_DMA_LEN0x1c unchanged if adding read-only capacity at the same offset; boot writes zero there.",
    "Keep existing logical pointer modulus and GPU_FENCE/reset ABI when changing storage depth."
  ],
